// Code-signing identity, supplied locally rather than committed.
//
// This project deliberately carries no DEVELOPMENT_TEAM of its own. The
// repository is public, and a team id belongs to whoever is building, not to
// the source -- so a fresh clone has nothing to sign with and Xcode says
// "Signing for 'solvr.ai' requires a development team."
//
// To build onto a device, create `Local.xcconfig` beside this file:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
//
// Your team id is in Xcode under Settings -> Accounts -> Manage Certificates,
// or via `xcrun xcodebuild -showBuildSettings | grep DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` on any
// project you already sign.
//
// The include below is deliberately `#include?` and not `#include`: the
// optional form is skipped when the file is absent, so a clone with no
// `Local.xcconfig` still opens, configures, and builds for the simulator
// instead of failing on a missing include. `Local.xcconfig` is gitignored,
// which is the whole point -- do not add it, and do not put the team id here.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
